//  BuildSettings.xcconfig
//  Capture
//
//  Committed. Sourced into the Capture app target's build configurations
//  (wired in scripts/generate_project.rb) so a value set here reaches
//  Info.plist through the literal $(POSTHOG_API_KEY) entry in Info.plist
//  itself, and is baked into every build INCLUDING an archive — unlike a
//  value read only from ProcessInfo.environment at runtime, which an Xcode
//  scheme's Run action injects but a device install, TestFlight, or CI
//  archive never does (FC-R14).
//
//  NOT an INFOPLIST_KEY_* build setting: GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE only
//  auto-emits INFOPLIST_KEY_* for Xcode's own known Info.plist keys, so that
//  route silently drops a custom key like this one.
//
//  POSTHOG_API_KEY below is committed on purpose: PostHog project keys are
//  public client tokens by design, and a fresh checkout built or archived
//  straight from the repo should ship with analytics enabled. The optional
//  #include? below still layers a gitignored Secrets.xcconfig on top —
//  xcconfig assignment order means the later value wins, so a local
//  override there (e.g. pointing at a different PostHog project) beats
//  the committed value below.

// Public PostHog project key — same value the portals commit in
// wrangler.jsonc; Secrets.xcconfig may override.
POSTHOG_API_KEY = phc_D6Rf7ZYD5L7cTCgP1aBIV6kgANIFGnsbEgoYPXpsaNG

#include? "Secrets.xcconfig"
